    <main class="main">
      <header class="topbar"><div><h1>Authority Levels &amp; User Profiles</h1><p>Define who can see, manage, review, decide and administer each GN Central area.</p></div><span class="draft">Draft assignments</span></header>
      <div class="content">
        <section class="notice" aria-label="Security implementation note"><div class="notice-mark">i</div><div><strong>Role design is ready; security enforcement belongs in the authenticated system.</strong><p>This page models the approved access structure and user experience. The programmer should enforce every permission on the server as well as in the navigation, following the Lighthouse Central pattern.</p></div></section>

        <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="roles-title">
          <h2 id="roles-title">Eight authority levels</h2><p class="panel-intro">Roles follow the principle of least privilege: users see only the information required for their work, and sensitive actions such as decisions, exports, deletions and permission changes remain separately controlled.</p>
          <div class="role-grid">
            <article class="role-card" style="--role-color:#16345b"><span class="role-level">Level 01</span><h3>System Administrator</h3><p>Technical administration, accounts, roles, security configuration and audit access.</p><div class="scope"><span>Users</span><span>Permissions</span><span>Audit</span><span>Settings</span></div></article>
            <article class="role-card" style="--role-color:#d7a642"><span class="role-level">Level 02</span><h3>Executive Leadership</h3><p>Full programme oversight, aggregated reports, approvals and final membership decisions.</p><div class="scope"><span>All dashboards</span><span>Decide</span><span>Reports</span><span>Export</span></div></article>
            <article class="role-card" style="--role-color:#2367a6"><span class="role-level">Level 03</span><h3>GN Programme Manager</h3><p>Day-to-day administration of members, applications, assignments, content and communications.</p><div class="scope"><span>Manage</span><span>Assign</span><span>Publish</span><span>Export</span></div></article>
            <article class="role-card" style="--role-color:#1f9a9c"><span class="role-level">Level 04</span><h3>Executive Committee Reviewer</h3><p>Reviews committee or assigned membership applications and records recommendations.</p><div class="scope"><span>Assigned review</span><span>Comment</span><span>Recommend</span></div></article>
            <article class="role-card" style="--role-color:#7a58a0"><span class="role-level">Level 05</span><h3>Accreditation Manager</h3><p>Controls accreditation cases, reviewer assignments, stages, evidence and final workflow.</p><div class="scope"><span>All cases</span><span>Assign</span><span>Score</span><span>Manage</span></div></article>
            <article class="role-card" style="--role-color:#4b7f95"><span class="role-level">Level 06</span><h3>Accreditation Reviewer</h3><p>Accesses reviewer training and only the accreditation cases specifically assigned.</p><div class="scope"><span>Assigned cases</span><span>Evidence</span><span>Score</span><span>Comment</span></div></article>
            <article class="role-card" style="--role-color:#287a55"><span class="role-level">Level 07</span><h3>Member Representative</h3><p>Uses member resources and manages only the profile and records belonging to their organization.</p><div class="scope"><span>Own profile</span><span>Own records</span><span>Resources</span><span>Events</span></div></article>
            <article class="role-card" style="--role-color:#8b98a7"><span class="role-level">Level 08</span><h3>Applicant / Public</h3><p>Views approved public guidance and, after verification, accesses only their own application.</p><div class="scope"><span>Public guidance</span><span>Own application</span><span>Readiness</span></div></article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="profiles-title">
