        <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="matrix-title">
          <h2 id="matrix-title">Section access matrix</h2><p class="panel-intro">A yellow marker means limited, organization-specific or assigned-case access. Final permissions should be stored as individual actions rather than one broad page-level switch.</p>
          <div class="matrix-wrap"><table aria-label="GN Central authority matrix"><thead><tr><th>Section / action</th><th>System Admin</th><th>Executive</th><th>Programme Manager</th><th>Committee Reviewer</th><th>Accreditation Manager</th><th>Accreditation Reviewer</th><th>Member Rep.</th><th>Applicant / Public</th></tr></thead><tbody>
            <tr><td>Programme health dashboard</td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="limited">◐</span></td><td><span class="limited">◐</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="limited">◐</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>All membership applications</td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="limited">◐</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Assigned / own application</td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="limited">◐</span></td><td><span class="limited">◐</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Record final membership decision</td><td><span class="limited">◐</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="limited">◐</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Member directory and resources</td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="limited">◐</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="limited">◐</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Edit member profile</td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="limited">◐</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="limited">◐</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>All accreditation cases</td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="limited">◐</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Assigned / own accreditation case</td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="limited">◐</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="limited">◐</span></td><td><span class="limited">◐</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Reviewer training and scoring</td><td><span class="limited">◐</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Reports and exports</td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="limited">◐</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="limited">◐</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Users, roles and permissions</td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td><td><span class="no">—</span></td></tr>
          </tbody></table></div>
          <div class="legend"><span><b class="yes">✓</b> Full access</span><span><b class="limited">◐</b> Limited, assigned or own-record access</span><span><b class="no">—</b> No access</span></div>
        </section>

        <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="controls-title"><h2 id="controls-title">Required security controls</h2><p class="panel-intro">These controls should be treated as part of the authority model, not optional enhancements.</p><div class="controls">
          <article class="control"><strong>Assigned-case enforcement</strong><p>Reviewers cannot reach unassigned membership or accreditation records by changing a URL.</p></article>
          <article class="control"><strong>Comment visibility</strong><p>Separate internal reviewer notes from comments that applicants and members are allowed to read.</p></article>
          <article class="control"><strong>Decision authority</strong><p>Recommendations and final decisions are distinct permissions, with named decision-makers.</p></article>
          <article class="control"><strong>Export protection</strong><p>Restrict bulk downloads and record who exported which dataset and when.</p></article>
          <article class="control"><strong>Audit trail</strong><p>Log sign-ins, assignments, edits, scores, decisions, exports and permission changes.</p></article>
          <article class="control"><strong>No hard deletion</strong><p>Archive records wherever possible; reserve permanent deletion for the System Administrator.</p></article>
          <article class="control"><strong>Account review</strong><p>Review active accounts and assigned roles at least quarterly and immediately after role changes.</p></article>
          <article class="control"><strong>Server-side authorization</strong><p>Navigation hiding improves usability, but every protected request must also be checked by the backend.</p></article>
        </div></section>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
  <script>
    const filter = document.getElementById('profileFilter');
    const cards = [...document.querySelectorAll('.user-card')];
    const preview = document.getElementById('accessPreview');
    const previewTitle = document.getElementById('previewTitle');
    const previewMeta = document.getElementById('previewMeta');
    const allowedList = document.getElementById('allowedList');
    const deniedList = document.getElementById('deniedList');

    filter.addEventListener('change', () => {
      cards.forEach(card => card.hidden = filter.value !== 'all' && card.dataset.group !== filter.value);
    });

    function fillList(element, value) {
      element.innerHTML = '';
      value.split('|').forEach(item => {
        const li = document.createElement('li');
        li.textContent = item;
        element.appendChild(li);
      });
    }

    document.getElementById('profileGrid').addEventListener('click', event => {
      const button = event.target.closest('.preview-user');
      if (!button) return;
      const card = button.closest('.user-card');
      cards.forEach(item => item.classList.toggle('is-preview', item === card));
      previewTitle.textContent = `${card.dataset.name} access preview`;
      previewMeta.textContent = card.dataset.role;
      fillList(allowedList, card.dataset.allowed);
      fillList(deniedList, card.dataset.denied);
      preview.classList.add('open');
      preview.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth', block:'nearest'});
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
